# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# eco-COBALT additions (ocean_BGC feature/gz-cobalt-merge: GZ-COBALT + COBALT-DVM).
#
# The merge registers 21 tracers that standard COBALT does not, all of them
# unconditionally and none with an init_value, so they would otherwise start at
# exactly 0.0.  Because this case runs with enforce_src_info = t, every one of
# them needs a disposition here or g_tracer_print_info aborts the run with
# "<name> : src_file is not set in the field_table".
#
# Initial condition from ecocobalt_tracer_source.nc (4):
#   nvmmdz, nvmlgz, nsmt, nlgt are live grazer biomass.  Zero is an absorbing
#   state -- ingestion, growth and every loss term scale with biomass -- so a
#   group started at zero can never recover.  Same reasoning as commit 2820776,
#   which stopped cold-starting the phytoplankton.  nmdz and nlgz are each
#   split 50/50 with nvmmdz/nvmlgz (pair totals conserved); nsmt and nlgt are
#   each a third of nlgz's original value, added rather than subtracted.  See
#   README.md, "Initial conditions", before running longer than a regression
#   test -- testing found the exact value barely matters.
#
# Cold-started at 0.0 (17):
#   The gut and metabolite pools are flux-through reservoirs refilled from
#   ingestion within hours, so 0.0 is correct and self-healing.  fedet_fast is
#   produced by egestion rather than by its own growth, and is inert anyway
#   while do_fastsinking = .false.  fedet_fast_btf is prog = .false., but the
#   src_file check walks diagnostic tracers too, so it still needs these keys.
#
#   Setting requires_src_info = f and requires_restart = f sends them down
#   MOM_generic_tracer's 'initialized by the tracer package' path instead of
#   demanding a GENERIC_TRACER_IC_FILE.
